{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mrf7r99bob0","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"MILESTONE ls20 level 1 CLEARED, win condition proven: match glyph then exit through door under target","summary":"FIRST LEVEL CLEAR in campaign history (door-probe script, 2026-07-10, 19 actions). WIN CONDITION (proven live, extends causal model v2 note-mrf7jpahab7): (1) visit the mirror switch at anchor (30,19) to set the bottom-left glyph equal to the top-box target (from spawn: ACTION3 x3, ACTION1 x3 — one visit suffices since the initial glyph is the target's H-mirror); (2) the wall ABOVE anchor (15,34) — directly under the target display, previously observed as a hard wall in 638 unmatched observations — becomes a DOOR when the glyph matches; (3) drive to (15,34) (ACTION2 x3, ACTION4 x3, ACTION1 x6 from the switch) and push ACTION1 once more: level increments (frame level 1->2, score 0->1), cursor teleports to the new level spawn ((40,29) on level 2), timer REFILLS to a larger bar (100 cells vs 84) with NO life loss (c8 stays 12). Also observed: arriving at the switch pauses the timer drain for that step. Level-2 board: new spawn, bigger timer; target/glyph geometry to be mapped. GENERAL ls20 STRATEGY: per level — read target, compute mirror-visit count to match, path to switch, then path to (15,34)-equivalent door and push through. Sequence used: L3 U3 (match) D3 R4x3 U6 (position) U1 (door). Total 19 actions vs 84-cell timer at 2 cells/step = comfortable margin. The full 41-run arc: infrastructure (runs 25-37) -> compounding (38) -> game-model reversal via board rendering (40) -> offline causal analysis (46/46 switch evidence) -> scripted 19-action win.","category":null,"tags":["arc-agi-3","ewm","ls20","milestone","level-clear","win-condition"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-10T17:32:34.847Z","vec":[-0.028186796233057976,-0.05653456598520279,0.055998168885707855,-0.04255058616399765,0.052169349044561386,0.0071054077707231045,-0.061205893754959106,0.05332